A||N||8||gtsonly||wet sanding||||5||
Z||000000||gtsonly||05-28-2001||08:54 AM||||What is the finest grit you go to when wet sanding auto paint. Once it is dull from sanding how do you dring it back to a brilliant shine? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||thomas_l||05-28-2001||09:11 AM||||I just got through with mine. The original paint was badly oxidized (way past just machine polishing) and I am not quite ready to repaint. If you use the searches for "paint" and "sand" you will find 50 different opinions about the subject.<P>I first tried some 600, but that cuts too fast and removes too much material at once. The first step that worked for me was first pass with 1000 grit. The final wet sanding pass I did was with 1500 grit paper. After that I used a high speed polisher with a wool bonnet and 3M Finesse. I have also seen high marks for Meguires swirl remover, but haven't used that product. After using the 3M I hand cleaned with California Gold pre-wax cleaner as the 3M spatter is very tough to wipe off. I finished up with California Gold Carnauba applied with the high speed polisher. The result is a crappy, worn out paint job that shines like glass  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Caution: while wet sanding the clearcoat will run off looking like watered down milk. When you get into the base coat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> the water color will change and you will go through it really fast. Also be careful with the wool polisher - it will eat paint too.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://fearlessdata.com/fiero/87GT_small.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||gtsonly||05-28-2001||09:24 AM||||I started sanding with 2400 grit and went to 6000 for the final. I guess I have not gone far enough seeing how I still have that milky color and not the red of my car. The paint is the original paint from 86 and in great shape but the nose has those fine cracks and it is driving me nuts. Thanks for the info, back to sanding!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||05-28-2001||09:26 AM||||     It got the white oxidation off? I might do that till I got the extra cash to get a paint job if it did.  <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||05-28-2001||09:49 AM||||Hi Chris, Long time no hear. Just be careful. Paint is easy to screw up. Just go easy on it. I just had mine repainted. It looks great. I don't remember yours looking bad either. I hope your just working on the bumper and not the rest.<P>How have you and the rest of the family been?<P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000005||gtsonly||05-28-2001||09:59 AM||||Hey Josh, <BR>  How you doing? your right, the only area I am working on is the nose. I got those fine little cracks on it. The rest of the car is still sweet. Eric at <A HREF="http://www.boomtastic.com" TARGET=_blank>www.boomtastic.com</A>  put it on his web page under the pics. He has other cars too, you should send him some pics of yours and he will put them on the page<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPs||||reg||1
